# Line endings: normalise to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# The project formats with Biome, which requires LF. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# and no .gitattributes, a Windows checkout rewrites files to CRLF, which
# (a) makes `biome check` fail with formatter errors that mask real ones, and
# (b) makes `git status` report phantom modifications on files whose content is
# identical. Pinning LF here fixes both, on every machine, without anyone having
# to remember to set core.autocrlf correctly.
#
# `text=auto` lets git keep detecting binary files, so images, the PDF and the
# lockfile are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
